  "implementation_hypotheses": [
    "a_scheduler_or_stateful_service_can_exist",
    "minimal_resume_capability_can_exist",
    "some_explanatory_state_can_be_exposed_to_client",
    "peek_runtime_semantics_can_be_defined_later_without_removing_peek_from_product_surface",
    "non_touch_surfaces_can_use_equivalent_interaction_mapping_without_forcing_literal_touch_gestures",
    "exact_same_card_cross_device_resume_is_not_required_if_daily_progress_sync_and_some_progress_inheritance_exist",
    "offline_use_can_be_allowed_for_authenticated_users_with_cached_state_and_content_only",
    "sync_conflict_resolution_can_use_server_authoritative_event_merging",
    "CloudBase physical-space canonical state uses database transactions so concurrent function instances retry read-merge-write conflicts",
    "mobile remote authentication uses challenge-bound SMS verification, short-lived access tokens, rotating refresh tokens, and revocable server sessions",
    "production SMS delivery uses a receiver-selected Tencent Cloud SMS or credentialed HTTPS webhook adapter configured only through runtime environment variables; fixed codes remain development-only",
    "mobile refresh is demand-driven before protected requests and serialized per session so one refresh token is never submitted concurrently",
    "mobile remote auth calls and authenticated fetch pipelines have a 15000 millisecond deadline; session replacement aborts stale requests, timeout remains retryable, and cancellation cannot become authorization rejection or mutate replacement-session state",
    "an authenticated v2 bootstrap read derives account identity from the active session and returns membership, daily progress, learning card state, nullable scheduler cursor, physical space, and content version without accepting phone_number input",
    "missing bootstrap components return explicit empty server state and never import device-local state; bootstrap-component-revisions.v1 exposes membership base-plus-beta, requested-track learning event-plus-session-plus-space, progress account-sequence-plus-check-in-plus-space, and account-space owner vectors without claiming a scalar revision or cross-collection transaction; the CloudBase Progress owner inputs are read in one transaction so its vector describes its returned projection",
    "generated_at and acknowledged_at remain observation and audit timestamps rather than same-millisecond ordering authority; content SHA and release identity remain scope identity rather than a fabricated monotonic revision",
    "bootstrap content version is derived from normalized ordered content; production fails closed without a matching published content-release.v1 descriptor, controlled_pilot fails closed without a current pilot-content-release.v1 descriptor and exposes its separate exact pilot content variant, while development may expose a null release id",
    "mobile remote login and restored sessions parse the exact bootstrap scope then fail closed unless the actual native ios or android platform and strict semantic version meet the applicable release minimum before returning or hydrating its canonical baseline; only then do they validate the loaded card-source identity and content version before enabling learning, persisting reconciled state, replaying mutations, or pushing product-state writes",
    "mobile keeps a still-valid authenticated session retryable after transient bootstrap failure but fails closed without previously validated canonical state and required content; reconnect reads canonical state before replay and again after replay",
    "bootstrap plus the repository-local learning-events.v2 backend, explicit v2 daily check-in, physical-space actions, React Native durable producer/replay, server scheduler, and mobile selection binding do not by themselves complete content-manifest release-key injection, receiver deployment, or CommonJS CloudBase production readiness",
    "the repository-local CloudBase learning-events.v2, daily-check-in.v2, and space-actions.v2 endpoints, React Native event/check-in/space-action clients, server scheduler, and mobile session consumer implement active-session identity, immutable account-scoped commands, durable queues before UI authority advances, exact replay, strict acknowledgement removal, retained content validation, transactional projections, canonical bootstrap reconciliation, server card selection, and global removal of v1 daily/learning/space snapshot APIs; deployment remains pending",
    "authenticated card-source and membership reads/mutations use session-owned v2 routes in every runtime; development-only v1 aliases can accept an active v2 session during migration, the v1 daily and learning snapshot-write routes plus both v1 physical-space snapshot routes are always disabled, and production continues to reject every v1 route",
    "remote content failures fail closed and never substitute bundled development cards",
    "an authenticated v2 content manifest is an exact formal-or-controlled_pilot discriminated union that binds exact active track content to URL-free audio descriptors, Ed25519 signatures, and private expiring downloads while requiring client byte-hash verification; the pilot variant binds exact android and ios semantic minimums, canonical future release expiry and gate_eligible false, and no pilot download may outlive that expiry; after strict signature verification the repository-local mobile runtime independently fails closed unless the actual native ios or android platform and strict semantic version meet the applicable signed minimum; the backend, strict runtime keyring consumer, exact mobile parser, native version gate, Learning binding, native content-addressed cache, completed-byte hashing, attached control, bounded controller, iOS AVAudioPlayer adapter, and Android Media3 ExoPlayer adapter are implemented, while production key registration, native release injection, private-object device playback proof, cross-platform screenshots, persistent receiver execution, and deployment remain pending",
    "closed beta premium access is granted or revoked only by a receiver operator through a dry-run-first command that atomically stores an idempotent audit event with the active beta grant record while leaving base membership unchanged; no client purchase or self-grant route is exposed"
  ],
